#   275 mm from the front wall face, with no landing; the g_front swing covers the only floor there; reduced with the
#   front door in front of the foot)
# expect: W_SWING_OVER_STAIR
# status: done
# fact: st (x 150-1050, y 200-3600, dir up) is entered at its south end y 3600 and the shell's inner face is y 3875: 275
#   mm of floor at the foot. d_front (x 300-1100) is hinged at (300,4000) and swings in with an 800 mm leaf, sweeping
#   x 300-1100, y 3200-4000: over the whole foot strip x 300-1050, y 3600-3875 and the flight's last 400 mm
plan "Front door swinging at the foot of the stair" {
  units mm
  grid 50
  wall id=shell exterior thickness 250 { (0,0) (5500,0) (5500,4000) (0,4000) close }
  wall id=w_v partition thickness 100 { (2200,0) (2200,4000) }
  room id=r_hall at (0,0) size 2200x4000 label "Hall" uses hall
  room id=r_liv at (2200,0) size 3300x4000 label "Living" uses living
  door id=d_front at (700,4000) width 800 wall shell hinge near end swing into r_hall
  door id=d_liv at (2200,1500) width 900 wall w_v swing into r_liv
  window at (3800,4000) width 1800 wall shell
  window at (3800,0) width 1800 wall shell
  stair id=st at (150,200) size 900x3400 dir up
}
